{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1511218-aether-and-aeon-aether-and-quantum-corruption","id":1511218,"title":"[Aether and Aeon] Aether and Quantum Corruption","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T06:58:45-07:00","id":1511218,"title":"[Aether and Aeon] Aether and Quantum Corruption","content":"We started this discussion before in other topic, but I think there is space for more\u2026 by the way, the subject is all covered with secrets from secret chapters, if I was to make it in a spoiler, I would have to cover the entire text\u2026 it would be too much.<br /> <br /> The idea is Aether is Corruption or at least a form of Corruption, what put Magogs (and Gogs as a extension) in the same field as Sub-Aberrants.<br /> <br /> Starting with Aeon, we have a few hints that Sub-Aberrants are not anyone exposed to Corruption, but a small percentage of the population.<br /> We could say quantum diseases are the real effect of corruption, as well as infertility and mutations to fetuses and seeds, what seams to be really normal (evil, but normal), as radiation have mostly this same impacts.<br /> Psions and Psiads being immune to direct corruption (but not corrupt microbes), we can expect latents would become slightly resistant to corruption, maybe even immune to the direct effects.<br /> Novas would slowly accumulate Flux and transcendence, and those that would become Novas erupt with high transcendence.<br /> Talents seams to be the best candidates to become Sub-Aberrants. Their body will fight to prevent death, mutating their bodies, by importing variations of themselves or activating all possible genes in their pool, becoming monsters themselves. Sure it\u2019s not an official thing, but we could go with this logic, exposition to Flux turn you into a Talent, quantum flux may turn you into a quantum corrupted version of a talent.<br /> All that to say Sub-Aberrants are a weird form of Inspired.<br /> On another aspect, the noetic scientists know Corruption is not exactly quantum, but what happens when too much quantum is used in a certain place, and the existence of non-corrupt Novas is a prove of that. So we can say there is Quantum and there is Corruption and they are not the same, but related.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant there are a few other ideas that go with that direction when you combine them with the other settings.<br /> We know there are Novas that don\u2019t have the MR Coils in their bodies, as the MR Coils are what make them capable of dealing with Quantum, they probably don\u2019t deal with Quantum. As the Nova Era scientists have no idea of the difference between Quantum and Psi, we can suppose they would call a Psiad a Nova, and the same with the most overt Talets, those with too much luck or skill to not be powered.<br /> Now with a leap, we can say Telecommunication Mega Edge is not different from the Aetheric Gift that allow Aethernauts to other Aethernauts directly with their minds, as both are limited to work with Inspired people. Sure, the explanation for Telecommunication is that it has something to do with Quantum, but if it works on any Nova it would work on Psiads and overt Talents too? Not clear\u2026 but Aether allow to do so, even if not using the same source. We know Sub-Aberrants can be part of hiveminds so we could consider Sub-Aberrants are Inspired somehow\u2026<br /> <br /> Now to Aether. First, we know Aehter have a strong connection to Quantum, it\u2019s actually Flux forced out of place by quantum. It by itself is an indication it\u2019s related to Corruption, but there are other signals.<br /> Magogs have been around for some time, there are two possible explanations for that, one they are Novas not aware of that condition, that have been experimenting with quantum for a while and end up capable of creating other novas or creating sub-Aberrants. Second option is they are indeed Magogs, and have found a way to generate Aether without accessing other realities.<br /> The first idea points directly to Magogs being Novas or Sub-Aberrants, or at least the older Magogs, and as they use Aether, Aether is Corruption. The second idea is that they created Aether, and so you can create Aether without the reality drills, and so it doesn\u2019t need to come from other realities to be Aether, or at least used as Aether, pointing Aether as a specific variation of corruption and Magogs capable of dealing with corruption as much as they would with Aether, making them a kind of Sub-Aberrant.<br /> It\u2019s also possible that Magogs, or those that would become Magogs, are actually accessing other realities, and by brute force creating small amounts of Aether, that is not corruption, but in that case they are dealing with quantum users of other realities (a good reason for Scholomance be known for dealing with THE DEVIL HIMSELF, is that HE is actually a Nove from another reality), but it kind of push back to the fact it\u2019s Quantum distorting Flux and creating a corrupt form of Flux, what can be the same as Corruption, but more attuned to the space between realities and less to the flux in a single reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:15:51-07:00","id":1511252,"title":"","content":"All I can add to this theory is... ( I totally agree with your assessments, and using my Sub-Aberrants as sorts 'cosmic Magogs' from now on. \ud83d\ude09 / Which is a bit strange, as Aberrants can be still looking normal in Aeon - only not sustaining it, most of the time... \ud83e\udd14) <br /> <br /> <img width=\"640\" height=\"424\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/bD9vHNiR1rQAAAAd/boom-mind-blown.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/bD9vHNiR1rQAAAAd/boom-mind-blown.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/bD9vHNiR1rQAAAAd/boom-mind-blown.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:19:59-07:00","id":1511263,"title":"","content":"Aberrants and SubAberants are two different things, and both can look normal to be fair, but a SubAb can\u2019t revert back once mutated, and a Aberrant can (or at least could maybe practice to do it\u2026 if train hard enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T20:28:51-07:00","id":1511323,"title":"","content":"As I've said repeatedly, you're misunderstanding what the Aether setting secrets chapter is saying about Quantum and Aether. The chapter gives the specific example of shoving an industrial saw through meat; Quantum energy is the saw and Dimensional Flux is the meat. There is no Quantum Corruption in the meat, the Quantum energy has simply transformed the meat into disgusting meat goop. To use an example of my own, Dimensional Flux is like the matter you see all around you while Aether is like the degenerate matter found inside a white dwarf star; on the one hand, they're effectively the same thing, but on the other hand, they really, really aren't. The absurd forces generated by the dwarf star may have caused the degenerate matter to form, but that matter and the force which generated it are two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T20:39:11-07:00","id":1511324,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t say Aether is Quantum or is Flux, I said Aether is one kind of corruption, and corruption is not quantum.<br /> <br /> It is a sub product of the use of massive amounts of quantum in a specific place.<br /> <br /> The entire theory is not much about Aether, but what Corruption is\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-10-2023, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"